<!-- SECTION 1: TECHNOLOGY MATRIX -->
<h1>1. Technology Stack Breakdown</h1>
<p>The MediCore HMS platform is built using a modern decoupled client-server architecture with high-performance real-time capabilities.</p>

<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 22%;">Layer / Category</th>
            <th style="width: 20%;">Technology</th>
            <th style="width: 14%;">Version</th>
            <th>Clinical Purpose &amp; Implementation Details</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Frontend Framework</strong></td>
            <td>React</td>
            <td><code>v19.0.1</code></td>
            <td>High-performance concurrent UI rendering, responsive state management across 5 clinical portals.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Programming Language</strong></td>
            <td>TypeScript</td>
            <td><code>v7.0.2</code></td>
            <td>End-to-end static typing, strict clinical data contracts (Patient, Doctor, Bed, EMR records).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Build Tool &amp; Dev Server</strong></td>
            <td>Vite</td>
            <td><code>v8.3.0</code></td>
            <td>Sub-millisecond Hot Module Replacement (HMR), optimized production bundling with ES modules.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>CSS &amp; Styling</strong></td>
            <td>Tailwind CSS v4</td>
            <td><code>v4.3.3</code></td>
            <td>Modern Daylight design tokens, custom healthcare glassmorphism, responsive grid layouts.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Motion &amp; Animations</strong></td>
            <td>Motion (Framer Motion)</td>
            <td><code>v12.23.24</code></td>
            <td>Smooth portal switches, slide-in clinical modals, heart-rate pulse animations.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>3D Graphics Engine</strong></td>
            <td>Three.js (WebGL)</td>
            <td><code>v0.187.0</code></td>
            <td>Interactive 3D organ telemetry (Cardiovascular, Thoracic, Digestive systems) and clinical hotspot markers.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Medical Iconography</strong></td>
            <td>Lucide React</td>
            <td><code>v0.546.0</code></td>
            <td>Over 200 high-clarity SVG healthcare icons (vitals, stethoscopes, beds, prescriptions).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Backend Runtime</strong></td>
            <td>Node.js</td>
            <td><code>v24.x</code></td>
            <td>Asynchronous, non-blocking I/O runtime powering the high-concurrency healthcare API.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Server Framework</strong></td>
            <td>Express.js</td>
            <td><code>v4.21.2</code></td>
            <td>REST API routing, JSON payloads, CORS security middleware, and web database explorer endpoints.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Server Execution Engine</strong></td>
            <td>TSX</td>
            <td><code>v4.21.0</code></td>
            <td>Native zero-build TypeScript execution runtime for server and database migration scripts.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Primary Database</strong></td>
            <td>PostgreSQL</td>
            <td><code>16.x (Port 5432)</code></td>
            <td>Primary enterprise relational database (<code>medicore_db</code>), JSONB telemetry, ACID transactions.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Secondary Database</strong></td>
            <td>MySQL</td>
            <td><code>8.x (Port 3306)</code></td>
            <td>Dual schema database support with seamless failover compatibility.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Database Drivers</strong></td>
            <td>pg &amp; mysql2</td>
            <td><code>8.23 / 3.24</code></td>
            <td>Connection pooling, parameterized SQL queries preventing SQL injection attacks.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Audio Synthesizer</strong></td>
            <td>Web Audio API</td>
            <td>Native Browser</td>
            <td>Medical chime synthesizer, emergency call light alerts, click feedback without external media files.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Clinical AI</strong></td>
            <td>Google Gemini API</td>
            <td><code>@google/genai</code></td>
            <td>AI-driven patient triage insights, symptom intelligence, and clinical documentation assistance.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<!-- SECTION 2: SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE -->
<h1>2. Architectural Overview</h1>
<p>The system follows a modern multi-tiered healthcare computing architecture:</p>

<div class="code-block">
[ CLIENT PRESENTATION TIER ]
  ├── Doctor Clinical Station (Telehealth, Rounds, E-Prescriptions, SOAP Notes)
  ├── Head Nurse Station (MEWS Score, Bed Census, Call Bells, MAR Records)
  ├── Hospital Admin Operations (Admissions, Discharges, Wards, Staff, Billing)
  ├── Enterprise Super Admin (Multi-hospital governance, Audit logs, System status)
  └── Patient Self-Service Portal (Anatomy 3D, Appointments, Rx Refills, Doctor Chat)
            │
            ▼ (RESTful JSON API via HTTP / Port 5000)
[ BACKEND API SERVER TIER ]
  ├── Express.js Application Server (server/index.ts)
  ├── Dual Dialect Database Adapter (server/db.ts)
  ├── Real-time Patient-Doctor Consultation Message Bridge
  └── Live Web Database Explorer (/db &amp; /database)
            │
            ▼ (Connection Pooling / Parameterized SQL)
[ ENTERPRISE RELATIONAL DATABASE TIER ]
  ├── PostgreSQL 16 (medicore_db / Port 5432) [Active Engine]
  └── 20 Relational Tables (846 Patients, 80 Doctors, 12 Beds, Vitals JSONB)
</div>

<!-- SECTION 3: DATABASE ARCHITECTURE -->
<h1>3. Database Architecture (20 Relational Tables)</h1>
<p>The database tier in <strong>PostgreSQL 16</strong> comprises 20 specialized healthcare tables managing all inpatient, outpatient, and operational workflows:</p>

<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 25%;">Table Name</th>
            <th style="width: 30%;">Key Attributes</th>
            <th>Healthcare Function</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><code>patients</code></td>
            <td>id, patient_code, name, age, gender, blood_group, admission_status, vitals (JSONB), allergies (JSONB)</td>
            <td>Inpatient/outpatient census records, telemetry tracking, clinical journey.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>doctors</code></td>
            <td>id, name, specialty, department, consultation_fee, rating, experience_years, schedule (JSONB)</td>
            <td>Physician credentials, specialties, fee schedules, consultation availability.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>staff</code></td>
            <td>id, name, role, department, shift, status, contact</td>
            <td>Nurses, pharmacists, lab technicians, shift rosters.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>beds</code></td>
            <td>id, bed_number, ward_name, type (ICU/General), status, patient_id, patient_name</td>
            <td>Ward floorplan management, real-time bed allocation, call bells.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>appointments</code></td>
            <td>id, patient_id, doctor_id, date, time, type, status, notes</td>
            <td>Outpatient scheduling, telehealth queue management.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>prescriptions</code></td>
            <td>id, patient_id, doctor_id, date, medications (JSONB), pharmacy_status</td>
            <td>Electronic prescriptions (E-Rx), drug dosing, refill approvals.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>medicines</code></td>
            <td>id, name, category, dosage_form, stock_quantity, reorder_level, price</td>
            <td>Pharmacy formulary, automated inventory reordering.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>invoices</code></td>
            <td>id, patient_id, total_amount, insurance_covered, status, items (JSONB)</td>
            <td>Hospital billing, tax invoices, insurance co-pay tracking.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>lab_orders</code> &amp; <code>lab_tests</code></td>
            <td>id, patient_id, test_name, category, result_value, reference_range, status</td>
            <td>Pathology diagnostics, imaging orders, lab technician sign-offs.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>messages</code></td>
            <td>id, sender_id, recipient_id, content, timestamp, status</td>
            <td>Bidirectional real-time patient-doctor consultation chat.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>sbar_notes</code></td>
            <td>id, patient_id, author_id, situation, background, assessment, recommendation</td>
            <td>Clinical nursing handoff documentation.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>mar_records</code></td>
            <td>id, patient_id, medicine_id, administered_time, nurse_id, dosage_given</td>
            <td>Medication Administration Record confirming bedside dose delivery.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>doctor_orders</code></td>
            <td>id, patient_id, doctor_id, order_type, instructions, priority</td>
            <td>Bedside clinical instructions (fluids, diets, oxygen titration).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>discharged_patients</code></td>
            <td>id, patient_code, name, admission_date, discharge_date, discharge_summary</td>
            <td>Historical archive of discharged patients and length-of-stay metrics.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>claims</code></td>
            <td>id, invoice_id, provider, claim_amount, status, approval_code</td>
            <td>Health insurance claims and pre-authorization processing.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>immunizations</code></td>
            <td>id, patient_id, vaccine_name, dose_number, date_given, next_due_date</td>
            <td>Digital immunization passports and booster logs.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>meals</code></td>
            <td>id, patient_id, date, meal_type, diet_type, calories, status</td>
            <td>Inpatient nutrition tracking and clinical dietary requirements.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>alerts</code></td>
            <td>id, type (Code Blue/Call Bell), location, severity, status, created_at</td>
            <td>Emergency notifications and critical bedside signals.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>audit_logs</code></td>
            <td>id, user_id, action, target_resource, ip_address, timestamp</td>
            <td>Regulatory compliance and security audit trails.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<!-- SECTION 4: SECURITY & CREDENTIALS -->
<h1>4. Security &amp; Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)</h1>
<p>MediCore enforces strict multi-portal separation. Staff accounts require official management-issued Gmail credentials. Unauthorized emails or incorrect passwords are automatically rejected with security alerts.</p>

<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 25%;">Portal Role</th>
            <th style="width: 32%;">Authorized Management Gmail</th>
            <th style="width: 20%;">Password</th>
            <th>Access Clearance</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>🩺 Doctor Portal</strong></td>
            <td><code>medicore.doctor@gmail.com</code></td>
            <td><code>Doctor@2026</code></td>
            <td>Clinical Station, Patient Rounds, E-Prescriptions, Tele-Chat</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>👩‍⚕️ Nurse Portal</strong></td>
            <td><code>medicore.nurse@gmail.com</code></td>
            <td><code>Nurse@2026</code></td>
            <td>Head Nurse Station, Bed Monitoring, MEWS Triage, MAR</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>🏥 Hospital Admin</strong></td>
            <td><code>medicore.admin@gmail.com</code></td>
            <td><code>Admin@2026</code></td>
            <td>Operations, Wards, Admissions, Discharges, Staff &amp; Billing</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>🛡️ Super Admin</strong></td>
            <td><code>medicore.superadmin@gmail.com</code></td>
            <td><code>SuperAdmin@2026</code></td>
            <td>Enterprise Governance, Multi-Hospital Command, Security Audit</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>👤 Patient Portal</strong></td>
            <td><code>medicore.patient@gmail.com</code><br><span style="font-size: 8.5pt; color: #64748b;">(or Patient Code: P-10001 / Staff-registered)</span></td>
            <td><code>patient123</code></td>
            <td>Self-service: 3D Anatomy, Vitals, Appointments, Doctor Chat</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<div class="callout">
    <div class="callout-title">Patient Portal Login Policy:</div>
    <div>Patients registered by hospital staff (in Patient Directory) can log in using either their registered Gmail or unique Patient Code (e.g. <code>P-10023</code>) with initial password <code>patient123</code>. Patients who self-register from the login page use their registered email and custom password.</div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 5: CLINICAL ALGORITHMS -->
<h1>5. Clinical Intelligence &amp; Specialized Engines</h1>

<h3>5.1 3D Anatomical Telemetry Engine (Three.js WebGL)</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Real-time 3D rendering of cardiovascular, thoracic, and digestive organ structures.</li>
    <li>Interactive telemetry hotspots reporting blood flow velocity (1.2 m/s), myocardial perfusion (98%), and organ saturation.</li>
    <li>Lightweight WebGL shaders tuned specifically for daylight healthcare aesthetics without high GPU overhead.</li>
</ul>

<h3>5.2 MEWS (Modified Early Warning Score) Engine</h3>
<p>An automated clinical calculation continuously scores inpatient deterioration:</p>
<div class="code-block">
MEWS = Score(Systolic BP) + Score(Heart Rate) + Score(Respiratory Rate) + Score(Temp) + Score(AVPU)
• Score 0-2 : Low Risk (Standard 4-hour monitoring)
• Score 3-4 : Medium Risk (Nurse escalation &amp; doctor review within 30 minutes)
• Score 5+  : Critical Risk (Immediate Rapid Response Team / ICU Code)
</div>

<h3>5.3 Real-time Patient-Doctor Consultation Bridge</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Direct messaging link between Patient Portal and Doctor Clinical Station.</li>
    <li>Fixed-height viewport architecture preventing viewport scrolling disruptions.</li>
    <li>Web Audio API dual-tone chime alerting physicians upon receiving incoming patient messages.</li>
</ul>

